11
00:01:25,703 --> 00:01:33,556
Before writing any code, I profiled. I ran perf stat with extended hardware counters on both VVenC and

12
00:01:33,556 --> 00:01:41,409
x265. The finding: VVenC had a ten percentage point frontend bound gap — twenty point six percent versus

13
00:01:41,409 --> 00:01:49,262
ten point six. Its CPU frontend was stalling while x265's was not. Root cause: seventeen per-module function pointer

14
00:01:49,262 --> 00:01:57,115
tables with no centralized dispatch. The compiler could not inline or optimize across module boundaries. I do not

15
00:01:57,115 --> 00:02:04,967
