16
00:02:04,968 --> 00:02:13,626
The solution was a centralized dispatch table modeled after x265's EncoderPrimitives. A single g_vvenc struct with one hundred

17
00:02:13,626 --> 00:02:22,283
forty-six function pointers across fourteen sub-structs. The syncToGlobal pattern: every module keeps its per-instance table for backward compatibility,

18
00:02:22,283 --> 00:02:30,941
then copies to the global table. NASM assembly registration infrastructure ready for hand-tuned kernels. This single architectural change

19
00:02:30,942 --> 00:02:39,599
unlocked the compiler's ability to optimize across module boundaries.

20
00:02:39,599 --> 00:02:47,623
Eighty-nine spec files, one hundred ninety-seven Mermaid diagrams, thirty D3 animations. Every function pointer, every data flow, every

21
