23
00:03:03,671 --> 00:03:11,955
I started at the bottom of the stack: the compiler's SIMD output. Methodology: write a standalone microbenchmark for

24
00:03:11,955 --> 00:03:20,239
each candidate, measure speedup over scalar, gate at zero point seven five times, implement only passing targets, verify

25
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:28,524
bit-exact with SHA256. Seven targets across five modules. Six passed, one dropped — rdcost_sad8 was slower than scalar

26
00:03:28,524 --> 00:03:36,807
